# rule.require.timeless-lessons

> a brief distills a CONCEPT. the chronicle that led to it is a DEMO and belongs in its own file.

```
$brief.md                  # the concept — free of episode
$brief.example=$slug.md    # one demo — dated, sourced episode
```

test: strip every temporal and session-bound word. does the claim still stand as what IS and why? yes → concept · no → demo: eject to `example=$slug.md` · merely gestures at a conversation (no date, repo, path) → delete.

smells: *"recently"* · *"this time"* · *"we decided"* · *"as discussed"* · *"yet"* / *"for now"* · 🔴 *"an earlier draft said…"* (delete).

an ejected demo owes: date, repo, path/branch · what happened · the cost · a pointer up.

a term `.reason` is already an ejection target: dated `.disputes` / `.evidence` fine; its own draft history is not. a verbatim wisher quote is a seed, not a demo: never tidy it.

blocker: an episode fused into a concept · a lesson that fails strip-and-re-read · a brief that narrates its own drafts · an ejected demo with no date, repo, or path.
nitpick: a demo with no pointer up.
false positive: a dated, sourced incident that is the shortest form of the claim · a verbatim `.said` · a dated `.reason` entry.
